<title>USA: Philippines raises bond issue in U.S. to $360 mln.</title>
<headline>Philippines raises bond issue in U.S. to $360 mln.</headline>
<dateline>WASHINGTON 1996-12-11</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Philippines' National Power Corp, a government-owned utility, said Wednesday it raised its bond offering to $360 million, from $200 million.</p>
<p>In a filing with the Securities and Exchange Commission, the company said that of the total, it will float $200 million as guaranteed bonds due 2006 and $160 million as guaranteed bonds due 2016.</p>
<p>The offering will be made through Salomon Brothers, Merill Lynch &amp; Co and Morgan Stanley &amp; Co Inc.</p>
</text>
